 − s)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZ4.Ωs_atoms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZ4.Ωs_atoms","kind":"theorem","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZ4.lean#L295-L299","doc":"`Ω_s` with every inverse on one of the atoms `s, 1 − s, 1 − ε(1 − s)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZ4.tacticChart_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZ4.tacticChart_inv","kind":"def","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZ4.lean#L286-L291","doc":"Proves `x⁻¹ = X` by checking `x * X = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZ4.tacticChart_scalars","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZ4.tacticChart_scalars","kind":"def","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZ4.lean#L277-L282","doc":"Closes a scalar chart identity after `match_scalars`, once every inverse sits on one of the\natoms `s, ε, 1 − s, 1 − ε, 1 − ε(1 − s)` whose nonvanishing is in context as `hs he ha hb hw`.\n`ring_nf` puts goal and hypotheses in the same normal form, so `field_simp` can find them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZ4.w_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZ4.w_pos","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZ4.lean#L269-L271","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZ4.Chart.pb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZ4.Chart.pb","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZ4.lean#L267-L267","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZ4.Chart.pa","@type":"LeanDeclar